hat the AC is not satisfied until expiry actually completes.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["vague/subjective terms present: as needed","AC item 'value_wo migration applied to prod.' cites operational evidence (prod) that lives outside the codebase; tag it [non-codebase] — prefix the checkbox text with [non-codebase] so the completion verifier accepts a recorded attestation instead of failing to find code proof."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["file_impact is empty"],"finding":"No file_impact declared on a leaf work ticket.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2b56a0701da43def","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"n6324407e6516f811","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Record the {path, reason} files this work will touch (e.g. via set_file_impact) so the attestation is scoped to them.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an explicit back-out/recovery plan: sequence version deletion (step 4) to occur ONLY after all rotations (step 2) are verified complete and consumers healthy, and document how to restore access if a crown-jewel rotation fails after the CHANGEME reset (e.g. keep a sealed break-glass copy until rotation is confirmed).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.432,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 1: 'RESETS each live seeded secret to the placeholder. This is intended'","Step 4: 'Permanently delete the affected object versions'","T4 remedy requires an explicit rollback/back-out plan, not mere acknowledgement of destructiveness","No back-out procedure is stated for a partial/failed rotation before version deletion"],"finding":"The plan performs two irreversible operations — resetting every live seeded secret to the 'CHANGEME' placeholder on apply (step 1) and permanently deleting historical tfstate object versions (step 4) — but provides no rollback/back-out plan if rotation fails mid-window. If, for example, the Gerrit admin password or opcert signing key rotation fails after the value_wo apply has already wiped the live value to CHANGEME, there is no stated recovery path to restore operator/system access.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcc98fad83db77ffd","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Steps 1, 2, 4","norm_id":"nc134d0c31a8a9605","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A crown-jewel rotation (Gerrit admin, opcert signing key) fails after the apply has already reset it to CHANGEME, leaving prod without a valid secret and no recovery path","tfstate versions deleted before rotation is confirmed complete, destroying the only remaining copy of a value still needed to recover"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Explicitly order the runbook so the tfstate-version scrub is the LAST step, gated on 'all secrets rotated + all consumers healthy'; and note a break-glass recovery (retain the pre-scrub versions until rotation is confirmed, since rotated values are already retired) so a failed mid-window rotation is recoverable.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"medium","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"hard","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the value_wo apply and the concurrent 'rubied' apply are serialized against the shared remote tfstate (terraform state lock / DynamoDB lock table and an explicit apply ordering) so neither clobbers the other's writes nor races the version purge.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"Coordinate with the SEPARATE 'rubied' apply that is seeding 4 new MCP-PAT SSM params so the state scrub covers those params too\"","Two applies touching the same s3 tfstate object and the same /rebar/prod/ parameter namespace in overlapping windows — the plan defines the scrub-coverage handoff but not write-serialization/ownership of the shared state during concurrent apply.","ABSENCE: no lock/CAS/ordering statement (DynamoDB lock table, apply-sequence gate) for the concurrent mutation of the shared tfstate."],"finding":"The plan mutates the shared remote tfstate (s3://rebar-tfstate-896586841071/rebar/prod/terraform.tfstate) and coordinates with a SEPARATE concurrent 'rubied' apply against the same state file and the same /rebar/prod/ SSM namespace, but never states how the two applies are serialized — no mention of terraform state locking, apply ordering, or a lock/lease to prevent concurrent writes to the shared state object.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb7a6abc021a375fa","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Coordination section + Step 4 (state scrub)","norm_id":"n5904d719d4b1f492","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an ordering/locking clause: run the two applies strictly sequentially under the terraform state lock (confirm the S3 backend's lock table), and perform the version-purge only after BOTH applies have completed and their scrub-coverage is confirmed.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the partial-failure recovery posture: mandate that the irreversible Step 4 version-scrub runs ONLY after Step 3 verification confirms every slot is rotated and consumers are healthy, and document the compensating-forward recovery (re-seed remaining slots) with an explicit `DATA LOSS RISK` note on the permanent version deletion.","cohort":["T11"],"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6987,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Runbook line 131-132: \"There is no back-out for the one-time state scrub or the secret rotation: rotated secrets stay rotated.\"","Step 4: \"Permanently delete the affected object versions\" — irreversible","No stated ordering guarantee that Step 4 (version deletion) runs only AFTER every slot's rotation in Step 2 is verified complete"],"finding":"There is no back-out path for partial failure and the destructive steps are irreversible, but the plan does not define a recovery posture for the state where the apply/reset succeeded and re-seed then fails partway. The runbook states outright there is no back-out for the reset+rotation, and Step 4 permanently deletes S3 object versions; if re-seed aborts mid-way, some slots are stuck at CHANGEME (consumers down) with no stated recovery beyond 'keep going'. DATA LOSS RISK: permanent version deletion in Step 4 is unrecoverable if performed before rotation of a slot is confirmed complete.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4aacb8812e8fa056","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Step 4; runbook §Back-out (lines 128-132)","norm_id":"nac325b0523216154","priority":0.2513,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Re-seed fails after the reset; several crown-jewel slots remain at CHANGEME and the operator has no compensating-forward recovery beyond ad-hoc re-seeding","Step 4 permanently deletes a state version before a slot it references was actually rotated, destroying the only remaining copy needed to recover a mis-rotated service"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reorder so the permanent S3 version deletion (Step 4) is gated on Step 3's clean state-pull AND a green consumer-health check for every rotated slot, and add a Back-out subsection stating the only recovery for a partial re-seed is to complete the remaining out-of-band seeds (compensate forward), never to restore a deleted version.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"medium","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"hard","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that the historical-version scrub (step 4) must run as the TERMINAL state-writing operation — after both the value_wo apply and the rubied MCP-PAT apply have landed and after all rotations complete — and specify which apply serializes first so the two do not race on the shared remote state lock.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.265,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Step 4: 'Permanently delete the affected object versions ... s3://rebar-tfstate-896586841071/rebar/prod/terraform.tfstate (bucket versioning, ~149 versions)'","Coordination: 'Coordinate with the SEPARATE \"rubied\" apply that is seeding 4 new MCP-PAT SSM params so the state scrub covers those params too'","ADR 0105 confirms MCP-PAT slots are value_wo (never in state), so the residual cleartext risk is bounded — but the scrub-version selection is still ordering-sensitive because delete-object --version-id enumerates a point-in-time version list."],"finding":"The plan coordinates the state scrub to cover the concurrent 'rubied' MCP-PAT apply but does not specify that the scrub must be the LAST state-writing operation, leaving a hidden ordering assumption: any terraform apply (rubied, or a terraform-driven rotation) that writes a new tfstate object version AFTER the scrub would escape the purge, and two concurrent applies contend on the same remote state lock.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f19b24b54b2ee2088","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Steps 1/4 and Coordination section","norm_id":"neaf03687d1a16ec9","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["rubied apply writes a new tfstate version after the operator enumerates versions to delete","a terraform-driven rotation (runbook path 2) advances state after step 4, creating a fresh version outside the deleted set","the two applies race on the state lock and interleave, producing an extra unpurged version"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an explicit ordering constraint: sequence the value_wo apply and the rubied apply serially (naming which goes first) under the single state lock, complete all rotations, then perform the version scrub last so the enumerated delete set includes every version containing cleartext and no later apply reintroduces one.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Bound the reset→re-seed outage window: freeze autodeploy and suppress instance-refresh/ASG replacement for the window, and define a per-slot re-seed-then-restart ordering so consumers are not left booting against CHANGEME across all secrets simultaneously.","cohort":["T11"],"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.615,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Step 1: \"the provider re-sends value_wo = \\\"CHANGEME\\\" once and RESETS each live seeded secret to the placeholder\"","Step 2: \"In the SAME maintenance window, re-seed/ROTATE every affected secret out-of-band\"","Runbook line 93: \"user_data.sh's CHANGEME fail-fast prevents a boot on a placeholder in the gap\" — names the net but not a freeze/sequencing to bound the window"],"finding":"The migration apply resets EVERY migrated secret to the CHANGEME placeholder in a single shot, and every consumer that boots in the gap before re-seed hits the user_data.sh fail-fast. The plan names the fail-fast as the safety net but does not bound the outage window: it does not specify freezing autodeploy / suppressing instance-refresh/ASG scaling during the window, nor an ordering that re-seeds each slot's consumers before the next, so this is effectively a simultaneous all-secrets outage rather than an online/staged cutover.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f83bacfe60141f6bc","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Steps 1-2; runbook §REMEDIATE steps 1-2","norm_id":"n209f52c2683f11d4","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An instance refresh, ASG scale-out, or autodeploy fires during the apply→re-seed gap and a box boots against CHANGEME and fail-fast-loops for every affected service at once","The maintenance window overruns and the all-secrets outage extends unexpectedly"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a pre-step that pauses the autodeploy timer and any instance-refresh/ASG scaling, and re-seed+restart consumers slot-by-slot (or freeze all boots) so the CHANGEME window is explicitly bounded and no consumer is scheduled to boot mid-gap.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows